  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5901.10 Basic life support (BLS)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5901.10 “Basic life support (BLS)” means fundamental medical procedures and the scope of practice in which emergency medical care providers at any of the following licensing levels are trained:\n\n(a) Emergency medical responder;\n\n(b) New Hampshire emergency medical technician-basic (NH EMT-B); or\n\n(c) Emergency medical technician (EMT).\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at Chapter heading for Saf-C 5900) #12790, eff 5-24-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5900.html"
}
